      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i guess. but the support stuff feels so clinical and fake. when i'm writing, i feel like the only time anything is actually true is when i'm touching that darkness. like, what if the void isn't something to fight, but something to finally embrace? i've been thinking there's a certain kind of raw, terrifying beauty in just letting go of everything. like the ultimate expression of an artist is to finally become part of the nothingness they've been writing about.",
